---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description="What this site collects, the cookies Google AdSense sets, and how to exercise your rights under the GDPR and the CCPA."
  lede="What is collected, who else sees it, and how to opt out."
  updated="October 24, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy covers {SITE.name} at {SITE.url}. For any privacy question or
    request, write to <a href={'mailto:' + SITE.email}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site collects directly</h2>
  <p>
    There is no account, login or newsletter sign-up, so no name or email
    address is collected simply by reading. Two features store a small value in
    your own browser rather than on a server:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Saved ideas.</strong> When you save an article, its identifier is
      written to your browser's local storage so the list survives a reload.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Text size.</strong> The larger-text setting is remembered the same
      way.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Neither value leaves your device and neither is readable by this site's
    operator. Clearing site data in your browser removes them, along with other
    preferences for this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    Serving a page requires a request to the hosting provider, which records
    standard technical information: the IP address making the request, the page
    requested, the time, the referring page and basic browser and device
    details. These logs exist to deliver the site, keep it available and
    investigate abuse. They are not used to build advertising profiles by this
    publication.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and the cookies it sets</h2>
  <p>
    This site is a Google AdSense publisher, and the AdSense script is loaded on
    every page. That means third parties, not just this site, process some data
    about your visit.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Google and its advertising partners use cookies and similar identifiers to
      serve ads, limit how often you see the same ad, and measure whether ads
      work.
    </li>
    <li>
      Google's advertising cookie lets it and its partners serve ads based on
      your visits to this site and other sites.
    </li>
    <li>
      Third-party vendors may set their own cookies when their ads are shown.
      This publication does not control those cookies and cannot read them.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can turn off personalised advertising in
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google's Ads Settings</a>,
    review how Google uses data from sites that use its services at
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>,
    and opt out of personalisation by many other vendors at
    <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">optout.aboutads.info</a>
    or <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.
    Turning off personalisation does not remove advertising; it makes the ads you
    see less specific to you.
  </p>
  <p>
    Most browsers also let you block or delete cookies for a single site. Doing
    so for this site will not stop you reading it.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    No separate analytics product is installed. Google Search Console is used to
    see how pages perform in search results; it reports aggregated queries and
    counts, not individual readers.
  </p>

  <h2>External links and embedded buttons</h2>
  <p>
    Links to other sites, including any affiliate links, lead to services with
    their own privacy policies, and this policy does not cover them. The
    Pinterest save button contacts Pinterest only after you choose to use it.
    The <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure page</a> explains how affiliate links
    and advertising are handled here.
  </p>

  <h2>If you are in the UK or the European Economic Area</h2>
  <p>
    Under the UK GDPR and the EU GDPR you have the right to ask for a copy of
    the personal data held about you, to have it corrected or erased, to
    restrict or object to how it is used, to receive it in a portable form, and
    to withdraw consent you have given. You also have the right to complain to
    your national data protection authority.
  </p>
  <p>
    The lawful basis for the technical logs described above is legitimate
    interest in delivering and protecting the site. The lawful basis for
    personalised advertising is consent, which you can change at any time
    through the links in the advertising section.
  </p>
  <p>
    Requests about data this publication holds should go to
    <a href={'mailto:' + SITE.email}>{SITE.email}</a>. Requests about data held
    by Google or another advertising vendor have to be made to that company,
    because this publication cannot access or delete records held in their
    systems.
  </p>

  <h2>If you are in California</h2>
  <p>
    Under the CCPA, as amended by the CPRA, you have the right to know what
    categories of personal information are collected and who they are disclosed
    to, to request deletion, to correct inaccurate information, and to opt out of
    the sale or sharing of personal information — which includes sharing for
    cross-context behavioural advertising. You also have the right not to be
    treated differently for exercising any of these rights.
  </p>
  <p>
    This publication does not sell personal information for money. Allowing
    advertising vendors to set identifiers may still count as sharing under the
    CCPA, so you can opt out using the advertising links above, or by writing to
    <a href={'mailto:' + SITE.email}>{SITE.email}</a> with "California privacy
    request" in the subject line.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site publishes home decorating guides for adults. It is not directed at
    children under 13 and no information is knowingly collected from them. If
    you believe a child has provided personal information, write to the address
    above and it will be deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    The date above changes whenever this policy does. Where a change materially
    affects how data is handled, the change will be described rather than
    quietly substituted.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
